1 NOTE {geni:about_me} According to Hindu scripture, '''Vasudeva''' (Devanagari वसुदेव, IAST Vasudeva), also called Ānakadundubhii ("Drum", after the sound of drums heard at the time of his birth),[1][2] is the father of the Hindu deitie
2 CONC s Krishna, Balarama and Subhadra. He was king of the Vrishnis and a Yadava prince.[3] He was the son of the Yadava king Shurasena. His sister Kunti was married to Pandu. Kunti plays a big role later in the war Mahabharata.
2 CONT
2 CONT ===Family
2 CONT
2 CONT *Parents: Shurasena (father), Marisha (mother)
2 CONT *Spouse	Rohini Devi, Devaki
2 CONT *Children	Balarama, Krishna and Subhadra
2 CONT *Dynasty	Yadava
2 CONT
2 CONT Vasudeva was the father of Lord Krishna. Devaki , daughter of the Yadava chieftain Ugrasena and sister of Kamsa was his mother. Please note that Krishna's father was called Vasudeva (with Va pronounced as V-uh). Krishna was called
2 CONC  Vasudeva ( with Va pronounced as Vaa) , which indicated his father's name (Vaasudeva means "of Vasudeva" per Sanskrit rules).May 17, 2015
2 CONT
2 CONT https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vasudeva
