2 CONT History
2 CONT
2 CONT Part of the armed forces of Surakarta were under the command of the Mangku Negoro (also spelled Mangkunegara). In February 1757 rebellious Raden Mas Said submitted his army to Pakubuwono III and sworeallegiance to the rulers of Su
2 CONC rakarta, Yogyakarta, and the Dutch East Indies Company. As a compensation he received a hereditary appanage of 4000 households on Surakarta territory. His dalem (palace)was built in the city of Surakarta. Raden Mas Said (Mangku Ne
2 CONC goro I (1757-’96)) was paid by the V.O.C. until the end of the 18th century. In the time of the Batavian Republic the corps was refounded in 1803. It was named the “Legion of the Mangku Negoro” by Daendels in 1808. As a result of 
2 CONC the surrender to the English the Legion was disbanded on 17 September 1811 but re-established on 13 Februari 1812.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Legion fought in the Java wars (1825 -’30) and in Aceh (1873-’74). It was valued to be one of the best corpses of Java and served to suppress insurrections in 1921 and in 1926. After WWII the Legion was revived again in 1949 w
2 CONC ith the name of Territoriaal Bataljon Soerakarta. It was transferred to the Republic in 1950.  3 
2 CONT === GEDCOM Source ===
2 CONT
